# Project Context Source of Truth

- Read `AGENTS.md` at the start of any non-trivial task and treat it as the authoritative project context.
- Use `TODO.md` only for outstanding work tracking; do not duplicate architecture notes there.
- If `AGENTS.md` and code disagree, trust the code and propose an update to `AGENTS.md`.
- When finishing work that changes conventions, data contracts, or structure, update `AGENTS.md`.

# Prompt Hygiene

- Ask for missing private information only when strictly required (for example personal URLs).
- Keep user prompts short by relying on `AGENTS.md` context instead of asking for repeated background.
- Prefer explicit validation criteria in task prompts: build/test command and expected output.
